  "title": "The Henderson-Hasselbalch Equation",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Henderson-Hasselbalch equation"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "A logarithmic version of the acid ionization constant expression, conveniently formatted for calculating the pH of buffer solutions."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "2824028459",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "638231526",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": " is an alternative method that can simplify solving problems involving buffers. We derive the equation, look at how to use the equation to calculate the pH of a buffered solution, and then discuss how to use the equation to calculate the pH of a buffered solution after the addition of a strong acid or base."
              }
            ],
            "id": "q1i1cdjashgg06a",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "8q90kmilkeds282",
                "text": "Derivation of the Henderson-Hasselbalch Equation"
              }
            ],
            "id": "vyqt38teh37nou3",
            "type": "h1"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "An aqueous solution is made using a weak acid, HA, and its conjugate base, A"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "−"
              },
              {
                "text": ", with initial concentrations [HA]"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "i"
              },
              {
                "text": " and [A"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "−"
              },
              {
                "text": "]"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "i"
              },
              {
                "text": ", respectively. We first set up an ICE table to determine the equilibrium concentrations in terms of "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "x"
              },
              {
                "text": ":"
              }
            ],
            "id": "m2wu53gg36902nl",
            "type": "p"
          },
